course: dictionary
lesson: 12580
title: Dine: a formal word for eating
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Dine» is a formal word for eating dinner, the main meal of the day. When you see it, think of sitting down to eat a proper meal, often with other people.
explain: «We dine together every evening.» Here dine means we eat our main meal together. You could swap in eat and the sentence would still make sense, but dine sounds more polished, like a book or a grand dinner party.
explain: Dine has two useful patterns. «To dine out» means to eat in a restaurant, as in «Mum and Dad dine out on Fridays.» «To dine on something» means to eat it for a meal, as in «They dined on fish and chips.»
fact: Dine is a verb: dine, dines, dined, dining.
fact: «Dine» means to eat dinner, the main meal of the day. It is a formal word.
fact: «Dine out» means to eat in a restaurant.
fact: «Dine on» something means to eat it for a meal.
fact: The words dining room and dining table come from dine.
exercise: «We dine together every evening.» What does dine mean here? | To sleep early | To wash the dishes | *To eat a meal | To sing loudly
exercise: «My parents dined out for their anniversary.» What does dined out mean? | They went to bed early | *They ate in a restaurant | They went shopping | They cooked at home
exercise: «The family dined at seven.» Find and copy the form of dine in this sentence. | seven | at | family | *dined
test: «The king dined on roast swan.» What did the king do? | He built a castle | He went hunting | *He ate a meal of roast swan | He sold the swan
test: Tom and Sara are going to dine out tonight. Where will they eat? | At home in the kitchen | *In a restaurant | In a park | In bed
exam: Which phrase means to eat in a restaurant? | *To dine out | To dine with the dog | To dine in bed | To dine on
